    "topic": "General Organic Chemistry",
    "difficulty": "Hard",
    "question": "Find the correct increasing order of stability for the four resonance structures A, B, C, D shown in the diagram: (see diagram)",
    "questionImage": "goc hard/goc_hard_q1.png",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "text": "C < A < B < D",
        "image": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "B",
        "text": "C < D < B < A",
        "image": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "C",
        "text": "D < C < A < B",
        "image": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "D",
        "text": "D < C < B < A",
        "image": ""
      }
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "A",
    "explanation": "Explanation: Structures B and D have complete octets (positive charge on nitrogen), hence are more stable than A and C (which have carbon positive charge and incomplete octets). Between B and D, D is more stable because negative charge resides on electronegative oxygen. Between A and C, A is more stable. Hence C < A < B < D. Option A.",
    "explanationImage": "",
    "marks": 4,
    "negativeMarks": 1,
    "sourceFile": "General Organic Chemistry - JEE Main 2023 January Chapter wise Questions by MathonGo.pdf",
    "id": 1,
