        "text": "(4)",
        "image": ""
      }
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "A",
    "explanation": "Explanation: Structure (1) is m-nitrophenol. The NO2 group acts via strong electron-withdrawing inductive effect (-I) at meta position, making it more acidic than phenol (4) and m-cresol (2) (which has donating methyl group). Cl is less electron withdrawing than NO2. Hence, (1) is the strongest acid. Option A.",
